              "date": "2024-10-22T08:35",
              "body": "Yearly physical, 51 y/o.\n\nInterval: no ED visits or hospital stays. Back unchanged; pain management still prescribing oxycodone 5 mg as needed. Omeprazole daily. Still drinking daily, roughly a pint; his wife has been after him about it.\n\nROS: no chest pain, dyspnea, abdominal pain, jaundice, hematemesis, melena, leg swelling or confusion. Sleep fragmented. Mood ok.\n\nPMH: chronic LBP, AUD, alcoholic liver disease (cirrhosis suspected on US 9/2023). Appendectomy age 11. Former smoker, quit 2018. NKDA.\n\nExam: VS as charted. Anicteric. Oropharynx clear. Neck supple, no thyromegaly. Heart RRR, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, nontender, no ascites, no palpable spleen. No edema. Skin: no jaundice. Neuro: no tremor, gait normal.\n\nPHQ-9 3. AUDIT-C 12.\n\nA/P\n- Health maintenance: flu, COVID, Shingrix #1 today (#2 in 2-6 mo). LDCT due, ordered. FIT kit handed over. Lipids and A1c with today's draw. Hep A/B series done, PCV20 done.\n- Alcohol use disorder / liver: same counseling; he would rather do it on his own. Labs today.\n- LBP: no change.\nRTC 4-5 months."
            }
